      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "ARTEMEX (4) struck a bit of trouble at the start from the awkward gate and drifted back to last on the turn before warming up out wide to run fifth over 1000m at this track two-and-a-half weeks ago. Has race experience on his main rivals and expected to go close. RED AFFAIRS (8) Home Affairs filly from Red Hearts on debut for the Sara Ryan stable. Has shown enough in the two trials to suggest a forward showing is on the cards. LAUGHING MOONS (7) three-year-old filly by Written Tycoon out of Khalama on debut for the Joe Pride yard. Strong through the line in her latest trial when second over 792m at Warwick Farm. Maps well and expected to take a hand in the finish. CHUMPAKIDD (1) resumes. Far from disgraced on debut when fourth over 900m at Newcastle last March. Ran third in a recent 816m Warwick Farm trial. Keep safe.",
